WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:10.380
The Second Wave from the supernova that destroyed the Earth...

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:15.950
Area of space in the southern ecliptic, approximately 40 astronomical units from the Sol System

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.300
...and colored the universe green 189 years ago...

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.330
...has approached the Sol system.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.720
Finally, the day after tomorrow...

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.770
...is the day of the Great Mission to protect the Earth.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.120
Papa... Mama...

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.650
Time Remaining Until the Second Wave Reaches
 the Sol System: 45 Hours

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.660
Episode Nine: 
I'm Going

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.290
The video you just saw was the final transmission...

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.270
...from the reconnaissance satellite launched from the Ultima.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.350
The Second Wave has finally contacted the Ultima.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.240
There are approximately 40 astronomical units...

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.380
...between the Ultima's current position and the Sol System.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.920
Peru - Nazca Space Port Current Time: 2:30 AM

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.810
At its current speed...

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:40.140
...it will take the Second Wave approximately 50 hours...

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.210
...to traverse 40 astronomical units.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:46.250
However, five hours have already passed...

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.430
Somewhere in Japan

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.060
Same Day, 8:00 AM Stellvia Central Control Center

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.720
...since the video transmission arrived on the Earth.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:52.600
Thus, there are only 45 hours remaining.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.160
There are concerns about the state of the Ultima...

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.250
...whose construction had been delayed.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.040
Shima-chan...

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.170
Same Day, 8:00 AM Stellvia Central Control Center

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.940
Final check for all of the generators onboard the Stellvia, complete.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.570
They are all go.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.840
Final check for each of the sub-generators at L3, L4, L5...

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.620
...and Luna, complete.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:19.550
They are all go.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:22.730
Estimated time the Second Wave contacts the Earth...

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:27.300
...December 19th, 4:37 AM, Sol System standard time.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.640
Notify all sections.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:34.240
The Stellvia Site of the Great Mission will be starting right on schedule...

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.750
...on the 19th, at midnight.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.630
Begin the countdown.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.970
Beginning the countdown.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:48.160
Same Day, 8:30 AM

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.960
Because of the shock that is estimated to come from the impact...

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:48.320
...please properly brace all easily toppled and fragile objects.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.180
...please properly brace all easily toppled and fragile objects.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.550
In addition, do not rush to the shelter, take your time.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:00.060
The doors to each shelter will be open until 11:00 PM tomorrow.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.560
We repeat...

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.340
...because of the shock that is estimated to come from the impact...

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.580
Is Rinna all right?

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.490
Her parents are on the Ultima, right?

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.510
Hmm, I wonder.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.010
Her face was really pale this morning.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.840
Being unusually sensitive will have the opposite effect.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.630
But because the Second Wave hasn't passed through the Sol System yet...

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:43.430
...we don't know if the Ultima is safe or not.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:47.950
That's right, I think that as friends we should just quietly watch over her.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:50.280
You can say that, but...

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.100
Hey!

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.550
Pierre!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.030
I-I'm sorry...

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.670
They said we're going to help with something else in the afternoon.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:01.970
Who did?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.190
Somehow, I have a bad feeling about this...

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.890
I object to heavy labor!

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.450
Same Day, 9:45 AM

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.650
All right, you're next, Katase.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.620
Fire your field generator!

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:44.860
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.650
Don't be frightened, fire!

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:05.590
Y-Yes, ma'am...

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.000
Shima-chan!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.570
I'll be repeating myself, but your duties...

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.470
...will take place inside of the Great Wall...

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.940
Same Day, 11:30 AM

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.900
...the barrier that will completely cover the Earth and the Moon.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:33.000
When localized parts of the barrier become weak and are penetrated...

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.370
...you will react immediately.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:41.590
So everyone has to be familiar with the flying plan of your team.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.580
Listen.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:47.110
The First Wave from 189 years ago was electromagnetic...

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:50.730
...but this Second Wave is made up of the pieces of the star that exploded.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.970
According to the plan, the barrier won't be penetrated...

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:57.030
...but we don't know what might happen, so we have to be prepared.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.510
We've mobilized all of the spacecraft...

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:02.060
...that are able to fly from all of the other bases.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.710
But the problem is that the only ones that can cover...

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.790
...the enormous 350,000 kilometer radius area...

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:10.560
...are the extremely maneuverable Ora-avis Machines.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:12.590
Which means that you are all the final shield...

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.940
...to defend the human race here on the Earth.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.460
I wish you good luck!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.440
That is all!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:31.730
Katase.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:32.970
Yes, ma'am?

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.980
What are you so afraid of?

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.720
It's true that even a single Ora-avis Machine is valuable.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.830
But you're a student.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.010
Your main goal is to acquire experience.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:54.490
Yes, ma'am...

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.060
If you don't want to go out, you don't have to.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:00.680
Think hard about it.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.460
Same Day, 1:55 PM

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.270
Everyone's already gone back...

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.430
Hey, big sister! How are you?

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:35.230
I-I'm fine, just fine! I'm doing great!

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:38.040
Well, you are following up being the leader in astroball scoring...

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.400
...with being the only preparatory student...

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.220
...participating in the Great Mission, after all!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.210
It's been crazy, your face has been all over the news across Japan...

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.190
...and across the world, big sister.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.140
You might be the greatest idol in the Sol System right now.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.570
Ho! Ho! Ho! Leave it to me!

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.680
More importantly, how are things there?

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.650
You haven't taken shelter yet?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.740
Our assigned shelter is right here in the neighborhood...

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.360
...so I guess we're cleaning the house up until the last moment.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.880
What? It would be better for you to hurry up and leave already.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.120
I'm sure that Chi-chan is dawdling and whining, isn't she?

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:13.240
Dad's asleep, but Mom's still awake.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:14.530
Should I hand her the phone?

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.110
It's okay. I mean, Chi-chan hasn't called me even once.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.250
I have nothing to say to someone like that.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.770
Cut it out already, big sister.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:25.720
Cut what out?

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.530
Come on...

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.270
Oh, well...

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.390
More importantly, what's wrong, calling at a time like this?

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:35.730
Did something happen?

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.580
What? No...

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.420
I was wondering if you had actually taken shelter yet, that's all.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:44.630
Dad said that maybe he would call tomorrow...

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:48.390
I'm sorry. Tomorrow I have to stand by from early in the morning...

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.300
...so I won't be able to take any calls.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.940
Uh... In that case, I'll go wake Dad up.

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:56.350
It's all right. Dad's tired, right?

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:58.280
And the day after tomorrow...

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.080
...we'll be able to call each other as much as we want.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.120
Big sister...

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.530
It'll be all right.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.770
Tell Dad to be sure to call me the day after tomorrow.

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:08.630
Okay...

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.260
Okay, then hurry and take shelter.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:14.390
The Earth is in more danger than the Stellvia, after all.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:15.920
Okay, goodnight!

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.500
Huh! Big sister!?

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.470
Shima-chan said she was doing all right?

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.050
She said to call her the day after tomorrow.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.530
I see...

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:32.060
That's right.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.990
Let's all call her. When the day after tomorrow comes.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.950
Same Day, 11:01 PM Local Time

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:37.660
Yeah...

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.480
Otoyama...?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.920
Wow!

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:14.770
Same Day, 2:10 PM

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.200
Why do we have to do something like this?

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:25.440
Or rather, isn't this robot supposed to be classified?

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.170
It doesn't matter if it's classified...

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.480
You guys came in here without permission, didn't you?

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:30.990
We don't have enough people to help.

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.760
Now stop complaining. Just hurry up and get it locked down.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.440
So we weren't punished then just so we could be used now?

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:38.450
That's right!

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:42.990
Milady, Pierre! Take care of the waste next!

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.490
Roger!

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:48.510
What's wrong?

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.000
Where are Dai-chan and Akira?

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.570
What incredible output!

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:56.520
Even ten times the power of a Bianca wouldn't touch this.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.550
Which means its hugeness isn't just for show.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.470
Oh. The arms and legs can move.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.160
Just what I'd expect from a giant robot.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.030
Don't slack off! Fire!

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:06.560
Yes, sir! 
Yes, sir!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.250
Pierre! 
Pierre!

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.000
Oh. They're doing it, they're doing it.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:15.260
It's Shipon!

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:18.150
Huh? Shipon, you're not feeling well?

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:18.960
What...?

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.330
Th-That's not it, not at all.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:22.600
Is it all right for you two...

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:25.440
...to be idling about in a place like this before the mission?

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.950
We're to stand by in our rooms until tomorrow morning.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:32.180
And when we went back to the school, Mr. James said you were all here.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.400
But exactly what are you doing?

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:35.880
Just as you see.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.020
We're locking down the giant robot.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:41.020
It would be really bad if this thing fell over, after all.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:45.420
But since it's a giant robot, can't you make it sit down?

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:48.750
Do you think we can activate something as dangerous as this...

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:49.960
...inside the hangar?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.850
And don't call it a giant robot.

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:58.720
It has a proper name - the Gigantic Actimo Soma Test Unit One, "Infinity".

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:00.760
G-Gigan...?

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:05.280
The Gigantic Actimo Soma Test Unit One, "Infinity."

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:05.950
Hmm...

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:08.670
All right, it's the Infi!

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.510
From now on, we're going to call you "Infi"!

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.240
Oh... It's started again.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:16.880
Hey, hey, Mr. Shirogane, what is this going to be used for?

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:19.020
Hm! I want to know that, too.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:20.700
It's for battle.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:21.620
What?

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:23.990
The containers lined up over there...

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:26.710
...are filled with the weapon options this thing uses.

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:28.490
All of those!?

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.330
Battle? With who?

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:32.780
With people.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:33.280
What?

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:36.900
This thing was created for when the Earth goes to war...

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:38.600
...with the other planets.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:42.360
War? Over what?

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:45.880
Differences in resources, immigration, trade, economics...

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:47.530
...religion, and ideologies.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.450
If you think about it, there are plenty of reasons.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:52.910
It's just that there haven't been any wars up until now.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.510
That's an unpleasant way of thinking, isn't it?

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:57.860
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:01.160
But why is something like that here?

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.290
The guys back on Earth built it...

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.920
...but they weren't able to handle it because it was over specifications.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:10.870
It's impossible to test it on the Earth, so for now, they've left it with us.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.100
Hmm...

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.770
It feels kind of like it's less than useless...

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.110
...especially the arms and legs.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:18.110
The face is kind of lacking.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.840
Save those for the person who designed it.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.600
Well, there couldn't be anything better than storing it away.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.750
And more importantly, right now we're doing the Great Mission.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:27.700
Shipon...?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.350
<i>Until the Great Mission Begins</i>

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.350
<i>31 Hours </i>

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.300
Man...

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:34.550
...those words sure put a damper on things.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.390
The sunset is completely ruined.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.780
More importantly, why the park?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.980
Same Day, 5:00 PM

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.460
A walk, a walk.

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:42.860
So, why?

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:44.500
Hm?

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.700
Don't ask why.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:50.340
You're always depressed these days! What happened?

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:53.920
The evidence is clear! Hurry up and confess!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:54.820
What!?

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.580
Did you confess to Kouta, and get told "I'm sorry" or something?

00:14:58.640 --> 00:14:59.820
That's not it at all!

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.270
That's not it at all...

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:13.390
I'm scared.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:15.440
Of what?

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.520
The Mission is... dangerous.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.570
There's that, but... if I fail...

